        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Tennessee",
        "text_sha256": "0f508660b269e506a0a8d75a779c9308c46be5b48e63a2ca187d6d91382ff384",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000041",
        "block_index": 41,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Texas",
        "text_sha256": "4b95ce6272018a31e4125bf2eb44817a30edbc954a0cf02d72c7c3cd08859373",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000042",
        "block_index": 42,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Utah",
        "text_sha256": "82bce10b5f88da7cb5c7ae0605298a1bc8145998b6363606e944d1ba4af409f4",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000043",
        "block_index": 43,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Washington",
        "text_sha256": "6b9031df058346a877deaba0a830b576fa81b9da8692e183e4eb4c9dc949054c",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000044",
        "block_index": 44,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How you can protect your child",
        "text_sha256": "2566057de328191457a528182043b391e9858008d1dd6a03d7ca5a83e8d571d3",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000045",
        "block_index": 45,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "There are several devices marketed to alert parents that there’s a child still in the car. A 2022 study by NHTSA examined many such reminder systems and found that results varied when tested in real-world circumstances. Trusted SourceNational Highway Traffic Safety AdministrationTesting of Unattended Child Reminder SystemsSee All Sources [6]",
        "text_sha256": "fd1e8df3575c0607aa3849c05314f3aa0842b570e92d55daec8fe4148f86d416",
        "word_count": 50
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000046",
        "block_index": 46,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceNational Highway Traffic Safety AdministrationTesting of Unattended Child Reminder SystemsSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "d1bee39429a79d9d3a53f402d2cb36d5f2d5cf5f96b44b7f8f3a8ef8ffb88be6",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000047",
        "block_index": 47,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "While some of today's cars flash a message to check the back seats, parents can take additional steps beyond relying on a vehicle's tech features. Safety organizations hope the acronym ACT will help prevent heatstroke deaths in cars:",
        "text_sha256": "7659bf3fb86016e0f06c6830dd1c2fc553a39e34b9fcf0fb59e2ef8ad4447cea",
        "word_count": 38
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000048",
        "block_index": 48,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "A: Avoid",
        "text_sha256": "caea66497bc870bf21e5ae2834e2ece5d749559a1817558d6558bb10bd23b450",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000049",
        "block_index": 49,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Avoid heatstroke-related injury and death by never leaving your child alone in a car, not even for a minute. Always lock your car when you’re not in it so kids can’t get in on their own, and keep keys and remote entry fobs out of kids’ sight and reach.",
        "text_sha256": "852fb4804221c506972c23627bba0a1f2ec5f493b2794e7b1f52a2136f39b926",
        "word_count": 49
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000050",
        "block_index": 50,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "C: Create",
        "text_sha256": "7aad3a0c78f2c0582e24643ddee89c2d8ae720d20a5ab11581789c93a4c52b69",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000051",
        "block_index": 51,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Create reminders by putting something in the back of your car next to your child — such as a briefcase, purse or cellphone — that you’ll need when you arrive at your final destination. These reminders are especially vital if you’re not following your normal routine when driving your child.",
        "text_sha256": "f4a52710d360d0ff1aced79bff66a7ed56761a75fe04998d54da4e407c1ea456",
        "word_count": 50
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000052",
        "block_index": 52,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "T: Take action",
        "text_sha256": "dce85180f01a2f5b6133f63c8450bad8dbc520033bef7e632080fdd6d0ad170e",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000053",
        "block_index": 53,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you see a child alone in a car, take action by calling 911 and following the dispatcher’s instructions.",
        "text_sha256": "bc3794ce88162d816061eabdc3ec833d1defd27424f4966e5af65041f45aeb22",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000054",
        "block_index": 54,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here are a few additional tips to reduce the risk of leaving a child behind in a car:",
        "text_sha256": "529032afca145483247390f94f0a161b71e6073c814506c8205484299216428b",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000055",
        "block_index": 55,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Set an alarm. If you’re in charge of dropping off your child at day care, school or the sitter’s, create a calendar reminder or set an alarm on your smartphone.",
        "text_sha256": "97a436d25a7bd9ffc6dc97f03fa17fe1170a4cac4095170e4930fe6b24816c23",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000056",
        "block_index": 56,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Ask for a call. Request that your day care, school or sitter call you and/or your partner if your child is not dropped off as usual.",
        "text_sha256": "35625131330446ddb7bb57448bb561518b00fa60710b2a0e611a99a62fccd783",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000057",
        "block_index": 57,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Tote a stuffed animal. Leave a soft toy in the car seat when your child is not in the car, and then put it in the front seat next to you when the child is in back to remind you she’s there.",
        "text_sha256": "06aa73f8166fc11d59d788fbbc533187aa34dd0b6a7c5cb5112e0fc24dacffe8",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000058",
        "block_index": 58,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Open the back door. Open the car’s back door every time you reach your destination to get in the habit of checking that you haven’t left your child behind.",
        "text_sha256": "fcb112dfaa950fa028be9ea8387929ac6472ae4185c5a00d3eaf443669b43f91",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000059",
        "block_index": 59,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "As scary as it sounds, keep in mind that hot car deaths are extremely rare and completely preventable. By resisting the temptation to leave your child in a car even for a few minutes and remaining vigilant by setting reminders to check the back seat, your child will ride safely — and won’t be forgotten.",
        "text_sha256": "eb3a69977da75ce67b2613843d4724060056b8a68fe0d1935a236c643bb158f6",
        "word_count": 55
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 1401,
